# Independent MW-01 walkthrough

Reviewer: /root/independent_design_review, nonauthor of production skills. This is a bounded semantic implementation assessment, not M2 or final Code Review approval.

The refreshed Codex, Claude and OpenCode candidate archives were extracted into disposable customer roots. Each contains only synthetic project authority/artifacts plus target support; the project does not require RigorLoop internal Design files. Installed resources supplied the common method, technical/composition reasoning, legacy feature procedure, architecture/ADR aids and independent-review handoff.

Result: the walkthrough supports the intended common/shared-owner and retained-source flows, with one corrected scaffold concern preserved in the initial report. The customer fixture artifacts and exact handoffs are in each target directory. The lease/worker/system example demonstrates one shared owner, a dependent consumer and an integrated commit obligation. Retry retains a substantive boundary-first-v1 amendment rather than forced model migration. Architecture/ADR artifacts retain their project-owned format.

Three complete JSON records pass the fixture schema. One after-record changes job identity, so the illustrated pair fails its invariant despite local validity. A separate valid example-only revision changes its exact hash while the parent hash stays fixed; the handoff includes the changed example, its owner and schema/counterexample evidence, and records required responsible-actor reassessment without automatic CLI invalidation. No actual old approval was forged: the prior-approval condition is a synthetic scenario.

Missing package guidance was exercised by deleting the required feature method in isolated copies: source contracts remained unchanged and the reviewer stopped dependent authorship for a distribution defect. A separate fixture demanded an unavailable customer-specific template despite a present generic aid: that is a customer-authority/input gap. A feasibility conflict between disconnected operation and current lease authority returns to the product owner rather than silently weakening no-stale-commit direction.

The initial installed legacy architecture scaffold named a retired Architecture review stage and contributor style path. The author corrected it. Refreshed installed guidance points to independent Design Review/exact legacy subjects and supplied styles while keeping lifecycle state in owning records. The old candidate identities and concern are retained in mw01-report-initial-candidate.json; only current relied-on resources were reassessed.

Limitations: reviewer authored the synthetic outputs while testing production guidance and does not independently approve those synthetic Designs. This is a manual semantic walkthrough, not a target-agent transcript or model-performance claim. Archive extraction is the installed-resource setup; real CLI clean-install smoke is separately owned. All30 selected fixture subjects were inspected by the CLI; those identities provide no semantic approval. Candidate/resource identities scope applicability and must be checked after subsequent edits.


