  "specs/retry.md": "# Retained Retry Contract\n\nboundary_contract: boundary-first-v1\n\n## Goal\n\nAllow a third retry without migrating this responsibility to a living model.\n\n## Requirements\n\nRETRY-SR-01: A valid completed-attempt count0,1 or2 MAY enqueue exactly the next attempt1,2 or3 respectively; count3 or greater and malformed counts MUST reject without another scheduling side effect. This scoped amendment raises the earlier limit2 to3 while retaining identity and existing contract ownership.\n\n## Boundary model\n\nBoundary model version: boundary-first-v1\nBoundary model scope: RETRY-SR-01\n\n| Dimension ID | Applicability | Governing requirement IDs | Boundary IDs | Non-applicability rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| input-domain | applicable | RETRY-SR-01 | BND-INPUT-001 | - |\n| state-lifecycle | applicable | RETRY-SR-01 | BND-STATE-001 | - |\n| identity-authority | not-applicable | - | - | This fixture amendment changes no actor or permission. |\n| composition-path | not-applicable | - | - | No alternate caller or component changes. |\n| temporal-retry | applicable | RETRY-SR-01 | BND-TEMPORAL-001 | - |\n| failure-recovery | not-applicable | - | - | No new recovery operation. |\n| compatibility-migration | not-applicable | - | - | Existing record shape and stable requirement identity remain. |\n| external-environment | not-applicable | - | - | No environmental interface changes. |\n\n## Boundary definitions\n\n| Boundary ID | Dimension ID | Governing requirement IDs | Partitions or transitions | Invariants | Outcomes | Owner requirement ID |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| BND-INPUT-001 | input-domain | RETRY-SR-01 | Valid attempt versus malformed value | Invalid input schedules nothing | Reject malformed input | RETRY-SR-01 |\n| BND-STATE-001 | state-lifecycle | RETRY-SR-01 | Available retry versus exhausted | No schedule after exhaustion | Allow third attempt; reject later attempt | RETRY-SR-01 |\n| BND-TEMPORAL-001 | temporal-retry | RETRY-SR-01 | Advance to next attempt or repeat exhausted request | Repeated exhaustion cannot schedule more work | Stable rejection after limit | RETRY-SR-01 |\n\n## Selected interactions\n\n| Interaction ID | Governing requirement IDs | Boundary IDs | Hazard | Required composed outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| INT-001 | RETRY-SR-01 | BND-STATE-001, BND-TEMPORAL-001 | Repeating an exhausted request schedules an extra attempt | Repeated rejection without scheduling |\n\n## Example ownership\n\n| Example ID | Classification | Governing requirement IDs | Boundary IDs | Regression ID | Discovery gap ID |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| E-01 | illustration | RETRY-SR-01 | BND-INPUT-001, BND-STATE-001, BND-TEMPORAL-001 | - | - |\n\n## Representative example\n\nE-01: completed count2 permits enqueueing attempt3. Completed count3 rejects; repeating that exhausted request enqueues nothing. The condition does not create behavior beyond RETRY-SR-01.\n",
  "docs/architecture/export/architecture.md": "# Retained Export Architecture\n\n## Introduction and Goals\n\nRetain the existing export architecture responsibility; add bounded retry behavior without model migration.\n\n## Architecture Constraints\n\nCustomer-authority permits the installed generic arc42 aid and separate ADR.\n\n## Context and Scope\n\nExport service consumes retry.md; see diagrams/context.mmd.\n\n## Solution Strategy\n\nKeep retries bounded at the owning feature contract.\n\n## Building Block View\n\nOne service and one queue; see diagrams/container.mmd.\n\n## Runtime View\n\nOn exhaustion return a rejection and do not enqueue again.\n\n## Deployment View\n\nSingle customer environment; release/publication is outside this amendment.\n\n## Crosscutting Concepts\n\nRetry state stays with its feature owner; diagrams have one text source.\n\n## Architecture Decisions\n\nSee ../../adr/ADR-20260908-bounded-retry.md for rationale.\n\n## Quality Requirements\n\nAn exhausted retry produces no new queue event; inspect at the queue boundary.\n\n## Risks and Technical Debt\n\nExact production capacity is unknown and owned by later Delivery evidence.\n\n## Glossary\n\nAttempt: one request evaluated under the retained retry contract.\n",
  "docs/adr/ADR-20260908-bounded-retry.md": "# ADR-20260908-bounded-retry: Bounded retries\n\n## Context\n\nThe customer needs one additional retry while retaining a bounded queue load.\n\n## Decision\n\nUse the amended RETRY-SR-01 limit under the existing feature contract.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\nUnlimited retry risks unbounded load; retaining limit2 does not meet selected direction.\n\n## Consequences\n\nA further transient failure can recover; exhaustion still produces no new enqueue event. Existing record identity is retained.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nDelivery allocates exact queue-observation checks. No current review or implementation approval is claimed.\n",
